<widget type="label" version="2.0.0"><name>label_367</name><text>whether the recombination correction is applied to the best estimate. True because an uncorrected recombination always understates the flux. Chosen in the 2026-11-14 plan; this reverses the earlier convention (old A19: the best estimate carries known, model...</text><x>590</x><y>241</y><width>552</width><height>50</height><font><font name="Default" family="Liberation Sans" style="REGULAR" size="11.0"></font></font><foreground_color><color name="Text" red="0" green="0" blue="0"></color></foreground_color><transparent>true</transparent><horizontal_alignment>0</horizontal_alignment><vertical_alignment>1</vertical_alignment><wrap_words>true</wrap_words><tooltip>recomb.apply_to_best: whether the recombination correction is applied to the best estimate. True because an uncorrected recombination always understates the flux. Chosen in the 2026-11-14 plan; this reverses the earlier convention (old A19: the best estimate carries known, modelled corrections only, recombination goes to the high bound). Confirmed by the user on 2026-11-16 ("Yes, keep it") (2026-11-14)</tooltip></widget>
