<widget type="label" version="2.0.0"><name>label_469</name><text>collection length along the beam = the electrode length, 50 mm (user, 2026-11-16, from the vendor figure of the split electrode: 50 mm along the beam, 63 mm across). The sigma is an allowance for fringe field and guard rings, which the figure does not show ...</text><x>590</x><y>187</y><width>552</width><height>50</height><font><font name="Default" family="Liberation Sans" style="REGULAR" size="11.0"></font></font><foreground_color><color name="Text" red="0" green="0" blue="0"></color></foreground_color><transparent>true</transparent><horizontal_alignment>0</horizontal_alignment><vertical_alignment>1</vertical_alignment><wrap_words>true</wrap_words><tooltip>ic500.l_eff_cm: collection length along the beam = the electrode length, 50 mm (user, 2026-11-16, from the vendor figure of the split electrode: 50 mm along the beam, 63 mm across). The sigma is an allowance for fringe field and guard rings, which the figure does not show (the guarded CMC chamber's l_eff was 2.3 % longer than its plate); it stays at 3 % until a fringe-field run says otherwise. The sigma is relative (0.03 = 3 %), not in the row's unit (2026-11-16)</tooltip></widget>
